# NOTE: a `.pubignore` *replaces* `.gitignore` for the directory it sits in --
# it does not add to it. So every rule the root `.gitignore` carries has to be
# repeated here, or build output ships in the archive.

# --- Mirrors .gitignore -----------------------------------------------------
*.class
*.log
*.pyc
*.swp
.DS_Store
.atom/
.buildlog/
.history
.svn/
.work/
migrate_working_dir/

*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.idea/

# NOTE: no leading slash on the build outputs, deliberately. An unanchored
# pattern matches at any depth, which is what keeps `example/build/` (GBs) out
# of the archive even though the root `.gitignore` anchors its own copy --
# `example/.gitignore` is still in force for that subtree, but relying on it
# alone means one deleted file away from a several-GB publish attempt.
pubspec.lock
**/doc/api/
.dart_tool/
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
build/
coverage/

node_modules/

# --- Published-archive only -------------------------------------------------
# Reference-image baselines: 64 PNGs, generated on Linux CI and only meaningful
# against that renderer's anti-aliasing (see .github/workflows/goldens.yml).
# They are three quarters of the archive and nothing a consumer can run. The
# directory goes whole rather than just `images/`, because `golden_test.dart`
# is the only thing that reads them and a suite pointing at missing baselines
# is worse than no suite.
/test/goldens/

# Commit tooling: commitlint and lefthook run in the repo, not for consumers.
/.github/
/package.json
/bun.lock
/commitlint.config.cjs
/lefthook.yml

# Tag configuration for `flutter test --exclude-tags golden`, which is a
# contributor concern -- the archive no longer carries the golden suite.
/dart_test.yaml
